<div id=3D"article-0-topx-0"></div></fbs-ad></div></div><section id=3D"how-=
ai-changing-critical-thinking"><h2>How AI is Changing Critical Thinking in =
the Workplace</h2><p>One of the most striking findings from the study is th=
at 62% of participants reported engaging in less critical thinking when usi=
ng AI, particularly in routine or lower-stakes tasks. Conversely, those who=
 had greater confidence in their own expertise were 27% more likely to crit=
ically assess AI-generated outputs rather than accept them at face value. T=
his suggests that AI=E2=80=99s role is evolving from a passive assistant to=
 an active participant in decision-making processes =E2=80=94 one that must=
 be evaluated carefully to prevent overreliance.</p><a class=3D"embed-base =
color-body color-body-border link-embed embed-2" href=3D"https://www.forbes=
